{{also|Malarkey}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|mallarky}}
* {{l|en|malarky}}
* {{l|en|mullarkey}}

===Etymology===
Of {{unk|en|title=unknown}} origin; perhaps from {{der|en|el|μαλακία||stupidity, idiocy, nonsense, bullshit}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|/məˈlɑɹ.ki/|lang=en}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/məˈlɑː.ki/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɑː(ɹ)ki|lang=en}}
{{rfap|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# [[nonsense|Nonsense]]; [[rubbish]].
#: ''I decided it was a bunch of '''malarkey''' and stopped reading about halfway through.''

====Synonyms====
* See also [[Wikisaurus:nonsense]]

====Usage notes====
Frequently, though not always used after "bunch of"

